---
import Card from "astro-theme-university/components/Card.astro";
import CardGrid from "astro-theme-university/components/CardGrid.astro";
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import heroImage from "../assets/images/hero-home.png";
import { courseMeta } from "../course-config";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../site-config";
---

<ContentLayout
  title={`${courseMeta.code}: ${courseMeta.title}`}
  description={courseMeta.description}
  heroImage={heroImage}
  heroImageAlt="A raked lecture theatre drawn as flat blue dots, one seat singled out in black by a sneeze-burst icon inside a prohibited-sign ring"
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <ul class="course-tags" aria-label="Course tags">
    {courseMeta.tags.map((tag) => <li>{tag}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2>What you will do</h2>
  <p>
    Each week you pick one public space — an elevator, a library, a queue —
    and apply the same method to it: watch the unwritten rule as it actually
    operates, isolate the smallest deliberate act that would break it, and
    write down precisely what happens next. By Week 5 that method produces
    Assignment 1; by Week 9 it produces Assignment 2; by Week 11 you perform
    a technique live, under supervision; and Week 12's Final Exam tests how
    well the method itself has stuck, on cases you haven't seen before.
  </p>

  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <p>
    Anyone willing to treat "everyone knows not to do that" as a claim worth
    testing rather than a fact to take on faith. No prior sociology is
    assumed. You should be comfortable observing strangers respectfully in
    public and, in Week 11, performing an exaggerated (not harmful) breach of
    etiquette in front of your own cohort.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to go next</h2>
  <CardGrid columns={2}>
    <Card title="Lectures" href="/lectures/">
      <p>What is covered, week by week, and which topics each lecture draws on.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Tutorial" href="/tutorials/">
      <p>The weekly activity that turns each lecture's method into something you do.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Quiz" href="/quizzes/">
      <p>A short check, week by week, on whether that week's method landed.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Assessment" href="/assessments/">
      <p>What is marked, what it is worth, and when it is due.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title={sessionLabels.plural} href="/sessions/">
      <p>The weekly schedule and what happens in each teaching session.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="People" href="/people/">
      <p>Who teaches the course and how to reach them.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Resources & Policies" href="/policies/">
      <p>Readings, referencing, slides — plus the rules on late work and integrity.</p>
    </Card>
  </CardGrid>
</ContentLayout>

<style>
  .course-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-block: 0 2rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .course-tags li {
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    background: var(--at-bg-alt);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
